  "Number": 1,
  "Question": "Makayla attended two meetings during her \\(9\\)-hour work day. The first meeting took \\(45\\) minutes and the second meeting took twice as long. What percent of her work day was spent attending meetings?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(15\\)",
    "B": "\\(20\\)",
    "C": "\\(25\\)",
    "D": "\\(30\\)",
    "E": "\\(35\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Use the same time unit for the meetings and the whole workday. The second meeting lasted \\(2\\cdot45=90\\) minutes, so the total meeting time was \\(45+90=135\\) minutes. The workday lasted \\(9\\cdot60=540\\) minutes. Therefore the percentage spent in meetings was\n\\[\n\\frac{135}{540}\\cdot100\\%\n=\\frac14\\cdot100\\%\n=\\boxed{25\\%},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
